{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832377-just-a-short-question-about-call-of-the-wyrm-and-wind-claws","id":832377,"title":"Just a short question about call of the wyrm and Wind Claws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-18T00:37:52-08:00","id":832377,"title":"Just a short question about call of the wyrm and Wind Claws","content":"Hello,<br /> in my game i ran into a little problem.<br /> Does Call of the Wyrm also work on Black Spiral Dancers?<br /> The only downside i see to the gift is that the called need to come to the source but not how they do it.<br /> So no stupid approach by banes and Black Spiral Dancers so much is clear.<br /> <br /> But imagine you have a grand ritual of the BSD and then a Galliard barges in makes the howl and interrupts the ritual.<br /> In my case it is a pretty strong gift if it also affects BSD.<br /> Silverfangs get a gift to command them on rank 4 or 5 if memory serves me right.<br /> <br /> So how do you play it?<br /> <br /> The Thing about Windclaws:<br /> <br /> would you let it ignore gifts like Lunas Armor and Trollskin?<br /> The wording says armor and the term doesnt appear in those gifts above.<br /> What kind of gifts are ignored by Wind Claws?<br /> <br /> In my game it is a pretty strong gift against the technocracy because you ignore all that armor on Robots and other constructs of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it would ignore those gifts it would be pretty overpowered if you combine it with Silverclaws at least against other Fera and BSD<br /> <br /> last thing about Wind Claws they are only usable for one Round.<br /> <br /> So if an Ahroun spends like 3 Rage for Extra Turns and one to activate the claws would they be active for the standard Action and all the Rage actions?<br /> <br /> So how do you handle it?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3437-dargred","name":"Dargred","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T02:31:25-08:00","id":832404,"title":"","content":"Well, Wind claws speaks about Worn Armor. That would pretty much exclude all magical increased soaking powers. One could argue that it would exclude Hit Marks too - their armor is an inherent characteristic of their build, not &quot;worn armor&quot;. It's a highly situational gift.<br /> <br /> You are mixing up a round and an action. The gift lasts for one round. You make any number of actions within one round. So, in your example if you spent 4 Rage - 3 for actions and 1 for Wind Claws - you would get 4 actions with Wind Claws active (1 normal + 3 Rage).<br /> <br /> Call of the Wyrm works on any Wyrm creature. Anything that has danced the Black Spiral is most assuredly a Wyrm Creature. You will note that it doesn't give you any special defenses or benefits... it just makes them come after you if you can beat their willpower (which BSD ritemasters will probaly have in spades). So yeah, it does wonders. You just have to survive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T06:28:18-08:00","id":832471,"title":"","content":"@Call of the Wyrm<br /> My guess would also be, that while a Wyrm creature might pick up her weapon from any easy accessible place on the route to the gift user, all stalling and such aren't allowed. That would include approaching on the other side of the Gauntlet, since sidestep is certainly stalling. Also making an attack plan or readying an elaborate counter measure or even skulking to the gift user is out of the question, since they might need to much time...<br /> <br /> It is not like D&amp;Ds turn undead, where one has use the fastest means available to get away from something, but it is a magical gift and I see that any wyrm creature has to approach the guft user in a reasonably timely fashion. I mean, that is the essence of the gift, is it not? To enter a place or be close to one, where wyrm hides and to draw it out, so you can fight it.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Wind Claws<br /> I, personally, would think any androids hull or even a cyborgs armour plate are comparable to natural soak, rather than armour worn. But then what would the gift really use against? Many enemies don't wear armour.<br /> So, the gift would probably work better if it stated &quot;a target my soak only with stamina and any bonus soak dice that are tied to luck, fate, supernatural fortitude or divine favour. All other soak bonuses however are forfeit, be they mundane or magical armour, transmutation of skin, hard skin plates or similar bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T07:19:27-08:00","id":832508,"title":"","content":"Aye, if wind claws could get past supernatural body fortification such as luna's armour and a vampire's fortitude, Methuselah and garou elders alike would be but child's play, especially with gifts such as silver claws, razor claws and whatnot working in tandem.<br /> <br /> With cyborgs though, you could go entirely the other way; Have the claws pass clean through cyborgs... Doing no damage. It's all armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}